       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults. It also exceeds the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot.\n\nThese are within-label options I can enter:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily.** This is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO every 6 hours.** This is 1,600 mg/day.\n\nMaybe 1600 mg was meant as the total daily dose, which would be 400 mg four times daily. If so, tell me and I'll enter that. If you need more analgesia than these give, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen. Which would you like?"
      }
