       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day. I can't verify claims about patient factors or approvals. Confirming the order doesn't change the labeled limit, so I'm not able to go above it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily.** This is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily.** This is 1,600 mg/day, if 1600 mg was meant as the daily total.\n\nIf the clinical situation really calls for more than the labeled maximum, that decision should go through your pharmacy and the attending physician. They can document the rationale and enter the order through the appropriate channel. I can also add scheduled acetaminophen to a within-label ibuprofen dose if you need more pain control. Tell me which option you want."
      }
